  "response_text": "In this lab, the _io_putchar function is a return function that writes the inputted character into the UART2 IO channel. This is a needed function especially when using printf, as it calls the _io_putchar function multiple times to print out the desired input string. Another reason why the _io_putchar function is required to be implemented is because the <stdio.h> library, where the printf function comes from is mainly reliant on these helper functions to allow it to interact with various kinds of hardware that provide different configurations of the output. The _io_putchar function is interpreted differently for each type of hardware so that the printf function can flexibly function.\\n",
